    "objective": "Fix the Coding-VP connector freshness deadlock in E:\\DEV\\Codex-web without weakening fail-closed semantics. Current condition: ChatGPT can successfully invoke real tools/call such as workspace_context against the target workspace, but platform schema caching may not emit tools/list/server/discover after a contract change, so Recovery Host remains connectorRediscovered=false and blocks acknowledgement forever. Preserve the invariant that ordinary tool success alone is NOT rediscovery. Design the smallest supported bridge/receipt mechanism that can prove the ChatGPT connector has observed the exact current tool contract, bound at minimum to client_type=chatweb, current process/server instance, and tool_contract_sha256, or otherwise provide a supported force-rediscovery path at the connector/bridge layer. Do not expose a new public business MCP tool unless absolutely required. Keep C4/natural-evidence gates separate. Preserve unrelated dirty worktree changes and .coding-tools evidence. Inspect both producer and consumer sides of the freshness contract, current tests/docs, and current runtime contract before proposing mutation.",
